MS (Mad Shift) quantization for llama.cpp
Copyright (c) 2026 Matthew Priester (https://github.com/devvexus, ORCID 0009-0000-0032-5292)

This fork of llama.cpp adds the MS (Mad Shift) weight format, written by Matthew Priester:
- the MS_C1..MS_C6 tensor types (bitshift-trellis coded, k = 1..6 bits per weight, 512-weight blocks) and their CPU (x86, ARM)
  and CUDA kernels;
- extensions of llama.cpp's prism.hadamard input-rotation metadata (per-weight block sizes and sign vectors) and their
  handling in the graph;
- split embedding tables and split output heads (msffn.emb_split_order, output_lo).

MS uses the bitshift-trellis construction and the computed "1MAD" decoding function described in QTIP (A. Tseng, Q. Sun, D. Hou, C. De Sa,
"QTIP: Quantization with Trellises and Incoherence Processing", NeurIPS 2024, arXiv:2406.11235).
MS's code was written independently and contains no code from the QTIP or QuIP# repositories; it uses the 1MAD constants as
published in the QTIP paper.

